═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

📊 WHAT GETS EVALUATED:

For each checkpoint, the 3D model is evaluated on:
  • Breathiness: 30 test samples
  • Roughness: 30 test samples
  • Strain: 30 test samples
  • Total: 90 samples per checkpoint

Metrics calculated:
  • RMSE (Root Mean Square Error)
  • MAE (Mean Absolute Error)
  • Correlation (Pearson)


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

📋 COMPARISON: PVQD vs 3D MODEL

PVQD Model (Single Task):
  • Trained on one task at a time
  • Separate models for each task
  • Evaluate with: configs/config_pvqd.yaml

3D Model (Multi-Task):
  • Trained on all 3 tasks together
  • Single model for all tasks
  • Evaluate with: configs/config_3d.yaml


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

✨ KEY DIFFERENCES:

PVQD Config:
  datasets:
    train_task_paths:
      breathiness: "...breathiness_train.json"
      roughness: "...roughness_train.json"
      strain: "...strain_train.json"

3D Config:
  datasets:
    test_task_paths:
      breathiness: "...breathiness_test.json"
      roughness: "...roughness_test.json"
      strain: "...strain_test.json"

Both use the same test data files!


