🎯 RECOMMENDED WORKFLOW
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1. Install dependencies
   pip install librosa scipy soundfile pyloudnorm

2. Test augmentation
   python test_augmentation.py

3. Edit config
   nano configs/config_pvqd.yaml
   Set: augmentation.enable: True

4. Run training
   python train.py --cfg-path configs/config_pvqd.yaml

5. Monitor training
   tail -f output_dir/*/train.log

6. Evaluate results
   python eval_multi_task.py --cfg-path configs/config_pvqd.yaml --ckpt-path checkpoint.pth

7. Compare with/without augmentation
   Run again with augmentation.enable: False
   Compare eval_results_multi_task.json


🐛 TROUBLESHOOTING
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Issue: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'librosa'
Solution: pip install librosa

Issue: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pyloudnorm'
Solution: pip install pyloudnorm

Issue: Augmentation not being applied
Solution: Check augmentation.enable: True in config

Issue: Training is too slow
Solution: Reduce prob (0.3) or use fewer types

Issue: Audio quality degradation
Solution: Use conservative settings (prob: 0.3, fewer types)


